suggestions.suggestionContent:
`isTeamAdminOrOwner` is computed with `&&`, but its name (and the intent of the authorization gate at line 54) is OR: either admin or owner should be allowed. As written, a team admin who is not also a team owner is rejected with FORBIDDEN even though they are a team admin. Use `||` so the value matches the name and the intended permission check:

const isTeamAdminOrOwner =
  (await isTeamAdmin(user.id, booking.eventType?.teamId ?? 0)) ||
  (await isTeamOwner(user.id, booking.eventType?.teamId ?? 0));

The `shouldInstrumentRequestSize: false` cases (CheckHealth at line 45, CollectMetrics at line 68) only skip the positive assertion; the body never asserts that the size metric is ABSENT for them. If the implementation wrongly instrumented request size for CheckHealth/CollectMetrics (e.g. someone moved/duplicated the `instrumentPluginRequestSize` call in metrics_middleware.go), this test would still pass. The field name encodes a claim the body does not check. Add an else branch asserting the metric is not present, e.g.:

if tc.shouldInstrumentRequestSize {
    require.Equal(t, 1, testutil.CollectAndCount(promRegistry, metricRequestSize), "request size should have been instrumented")
    require.NoError(t, checkHistogram(promRegistry, metricRequestSize, map[string]string{
        "plugin_id": pluginID,
        "endpoint":  tc.expEndpoint,
        "target":    string(backendplugin.TargetUnknown),
        "source":    "grafana-backend",
    }), "request size should have been instrumented")
} else {
    require.Equal(t, 0, testutil.CollectAndCount(promRegistry, metricRequestSize), "request size should not have been instrumented")
}
